{"step_index":347,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-02T08:22:58Z","thinking":"The output `\"TEST_VAL_123\"` provides a crucial clue; it's likely the direct cause. The update script's blind append operation, combined with the zone file's `$ORIGIN` directive for `private.sfrcaraibe.fr.`, causes new records to be placed under the wrong domain. This explains why the update fails, appending records incorrectly to the \"private\" subdomain. The original working record must have been correctly configured, but a later change broke this configuration.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"ssh ns1 'sudo sed -i \\\"s/_acme-challenge.geo\\\\t60\\\\tTXT/_acme-challenge.geo.sfrcaraibe.fr.\\\\t60\\\\tTXT/\\\" /var/named/sfrcaraibe.fr && sudo rndc reload sfrcaraibe.fr' <<< \\\"3?z7Q6}X39s>sWVA*t!h\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"/home/koby/LINUX\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Testing FQDN in zonefile on ns1\"","toolSummary":"\"Testing absolute FQDN with trailing dot in zonefile\""}}]}
