{"step_index":409,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-02T10:53:51Z","content":"Here is a briefing of the architecture, workflow, and operational flow implemented in [playbooks/issue-deploy-certs.yml](file:///home/koby/LINUX/playbooks/issue-deploy-certs.yml).\n\n---\n\n### 1. High-Level Architecture & Purpose\n\n* **Objective**: Automate DNS-01 Let's Encrypt certificate issuance, renewal, and target server deployment.\n* **Why DNS-01**: Inbound HTTP (`:80`) is blocked from the Internet on internal production servers, preventing HTTP-01 challenges. DNS-01 requires no open inbound ports.\n* **Zero Service Interruption**: Web servers are reloaded **only if the certificate's serial number actually changed** between pre-issuance and post-issuance checks.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Supported DNS Backends\n\n| Backend | DNS Server | Mechanism | Use Case |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **`rfc2136`** | BIND | Dynamic DNS update via TSIG key and `certbot-dns-rfc2136` plugin | BIND with TSIG enabled |\n| **`powerdns`** | `th2-dnsp-mst1` (`172.30.198.162:30`) | Passwordless SSH executing `pdnsutil replace-rrset` & `increase-serial` | Modern public zones (`outremer-telecom.fr`, `redcaraibe.fr`, `3gppnetwork.org`) |\n| **`ssh_zonefile`** | `ns1` (`172.16.75.250`) | Passwordless SSH executing [acme-zone-update.sh](file:///home/koby/LINUX/playbooks/files/ns1-hooks/acme-zone-update.sh) to edit zone files in `/var/named/` + `rndc reload` | Legacy BIND zones (`sfrcaraibe.fr`, `only.fr`) |\n\n---\n\n### 3. Execution Modes & Safety Guardrails\n\n1. **Catalog Mode**:\n   - Domains are defined in [playbooks/group_vars/all/certificates.yml](file:///home/koby/LINUX/playbooks/group_vars/all/certificates.yml).\n   - Filter single domains using `-e certs_filter=<domain>`.\n2. **Ad-Hoc Mode**:\n   - Target any domain on `ns1` without editing `certificates.yml`: `-e cert_domain=<domain>`.\n   - The playbook automatically discovers the hosting zone and file path via [find-zone.sh](file:///home/koby/LINUX/playbooks/files/ns1-hooks/find-zone.sh) reading `/etc/named.conf` on `ns1`.\n3. **Staging Guardrail**:\n   - `letsencrypt_staging: true` by default (`--test-cert`).\n   \n<truncated 1673 bytes>\n> T[\"Skip Reload (No Changes)\"]\n    end\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Task Breakdown\n\n#### Phase 1: Environment & Secret Provisioning (`tags: [always]`)\n1. **Package Provisioning**: Ensures `certbot`, `python3-certbot-dns-rfc2136`, `bind9-dnsutils`, `curl`, and `jq` are present on `localhost`.\n2. **Hook Scripts & Secrets**:\n   - Deploys RFC2136 credentials (`rfc2136.ini`), PowerDNS hooks (`pdns-auth-hook.sh`, `pdns-cleanup-hook.sh`), or `ns1` zonefile hooks into `/root/.secrets/certbot/` (`0700`).\n   - Copies `acme-zone-update.sh` and `find-zone.sh` to `ns1` via SCP if `ssh_zonefile` is in use.\n3. **Root SSH Setup**: Configures `/root/.ssh/config` and keys so Certbot (running as root) can interact with `ns1` and `th2-dnsp-mst1`.\n\n#### Phase 2: ACME DNS-01 Challenge & Issuance (`tags: [issue]`)\n1. **Pre-Issuance Serial Capture**: Runs `openssl x509 -noout -serial` on `/etc/letsencrypt/live/<domain>/cert.pem` to capture the current serial (if it exists).\n2. **Certbot Invocation**:\n   - Executes `certbot certonly --manual --preferred-challenges dns`.\n   - The `--manual-auth-hook` adds the `_acme-challenge.<fqdn>.` TXT record (with absolute FQDN to avoid `$ORIGIN` conflicts) and increments the SOA serial.\n   - **DoH Verification**: Polls `dns.google` and `cloudflare-dns.com` until both resolvers return the validation string consecutively.\n   - Let's Encrypt verifies the record and delivers the signed certificate chain.\n   - The `--manual-cleanup-hook` deletes the challenge record and bumps the serial again.\n3. **Post-Issuance Serial Compare**: Compares new vs. old serial. If different, flags `changed: true` in `certs_deploy_queue`.\n\n#### Phase 3: Deployment & Safe Reload (`tags: [deploy]`)\n1. Filters `certs_deploy_queue` where `changed == true`.\n2. Connects to `target_host` via Ansible delegation:\n   - Creates destination directory (`cert_dest_dir`, e.g. `/etc/nginx/ssl/<domain>`).\n   - Copies `fullchain.pem` (`0644`) and `privkey.pem` (`0600`).\n   - Reissues a graceful service reload (`service_name`, e.g., `nginx` or `apache2`).","thinking":"The playbook automates certificate management, specifically issuance, renewal, and optional deployment, using DNS-01 challenges. It's designed for environments where direct inbound connections on port 80 might not be available. The structure likely encompasses tasks to obtain certificates and then potentially deploy them.\n\n\nThe system leverages DNS-01 challenges due to the blocked HTTP-01. Deployment reloads web servers only upon serial number changes, ensuring zero-downtime operations. Different DNS backends are supported, including BIND, PowerDNS, and a legacy SSH-based BIND, each handled with specific logic for record updates and propagation verification.\n\nTwo execution modes exist: catalog mode for declared domains and ad-hoc mode for one-off requests. Staging environments are used by default with an explicit override required for production, protecting against rate limits.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
